Director, Sales Engineering (Southern Europe) &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ping Identity:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Ping Identity, we believe in making digital experiences both secure and seamless for all users, without compromise. We call this digital freedom. And it&#39;s not just something we provide our customers. It&#39;s something that inspires our company. People don&#39;t come here to join a culture that&#39;s built on digital freedom. They come to cultivate it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our intelligent, cloud identity platform lets people shop, work, bank, and interact wherever and however they want. Without friction. Without fear.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While protecting digital identities is at the core of our technology, protecting individual identities is at the core of our culture.&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pingidentity.com/en/company/championing-every-identity.html&quot;&gt;We champion every identity.&lt;/a&gt; One of our core values, Respect Individuality, reminds us to celebrate differences so you are empowered to bring your authentic self to work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re headquartered in Denver, Colorado and we have offices and employees around the globe. We serve the largest, most demanding enterprises worldwide, including more than half of the Fortune 100. At Ping Identity, we&#39;re changing the way people and businesses think about cybersecurity, digital experiences, and identity and access management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Ping Identity, we believe in making digital experiences both secure and seamless for all users, without compromise. We call this digital freedom. And it&#39;s not just something we provide our customers. It&#39;s something that inspires our company. People don&#39;t come here to join a culture that&#39;s built on digital freedom. They come to cultivate it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our intelligent, cloud identity platform lets people shop, work, bank, and interact wherever and however they want. Without friction. Without fear.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While protecting digital identities is at the core of our technology, protecting individual identities is at the core of our culture. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pingidentity.com/en/company/championing-every-identity.html&quot;&gt;We champion every identity.&lt;/a&gt; One of our core values, Respect Individuality, reminds us to celebrate differences so you are empowered to bring your authentic self to work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re headquartered in Denver, Colorado and we have offices and employees around the globe. We serve the largest, most demanding enterprises worldwide, including more than half of the Fortune 100. At Ping Identity, we&#39;re changing the way people and businesses think about cybersecurity, digital experiences, and identity and access management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Director of Sales Engineering, Southern Europe you will take a senior role in shaping how we engage with customers, partners, and the wider sales organisation. You will lead a small team of Sales Engineers, guiding their development and ensuring they are well equipped to succeed, while continuing to spend most of your time working directly on high value opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior hands on leadership role. You will set technical direction for key accounts, influence deal strategy, and help resolve complex architectural questions. You will act as a trusted advisor to customers and sales teams, while also representing the SE function in regional planning, forecasting, and cross functional discussions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead by example, taking ownership of strategic opportunities and stepping in where your experience can make a meaningful difference to outcomes. At the same time, you will coach your team to grow their own expertise and confidence, creating an environment where they can perform at a high level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Main Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Team Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and support a team of Sales Engineers (SE&#39;s), providing coaching, regular feedback, and career development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear expectations for technical quality, customer engagement, and opportunity execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help onboard and mentor new team members and strengthen consistent ways of working across the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with regional sales leadership to ensure SE resources are aligned with priority accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a healthy, collaborative team culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of strategic and complex opportunities that benefit from senior technical leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver solution demonstrations, discovery sessions, technical guidance, RFx responses, and proofs of concept&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide technical strategy across multiple deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an escalation point for technical challenges during critical deal phases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with customers and partners, becoming a technical advisor they rely on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with sales teams throughout qualification, discovery, and technical proof phases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate pre sales efforts with post sales delivery teams to ensure smooth handovers and clear expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Ping Identity at customer meetings, executive briefings, partner events, and industry sessions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross Functional Influence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide insight into market trends, customer challenges, and developing areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share well reasoned product feedback with product owners and help shape regional solution positioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support strategic planning and forecasting discussions with regional sales leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with marketing and product teams to refine competitive messaging and technical narratives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience of&amp;nbsp;managing sales engineering teams in France, and preferably also Iberia &amp;amp; Italy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of IAM concepts, architectures, and protocols. Experience with standards such as OAuth, OIDC, SAML, and SCIM is helpful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with REST APIs and JSON, and familiarity with one or more modern programming or scripting languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of core infrastructure technologies, including networking, DNS, HTTP/S, load balancing, proxies, and virtualisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with major cloud platforms, such as AWS, Azure, or GCP, and deployment technologies like Kubernetes and Terraform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of how customers are using agentic AI and how identity secures AI agents, their permissions, and their behaviour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, including the ability to explain technical concepts clearly to technical and non technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently while also supporting and elevating a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable managing multiple priorities without losing focus on key opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine interest in learning and staying current in a fast evolving technical landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS in Software Engineering or equivalent degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent French language skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligibility to work in France&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at Ping:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in and facilitate a flexible, collaborative work environment. We’re growing quickly, but remain true to the innovative, can-do startup values that got us here. Most importantly, we keep hiring talented, smart, fun, and genuinely nice people because that’s who we want to succeed with every day.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here are just a few of the things that make Ping special:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A company culture that empowers you to do your best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Resource Groups that create a sense of belonging for everyone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular company and team bonding events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive benefits and perks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global volunteering and community initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Benefits:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous PTO &amp;amp; Holiday Schedule&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progressive Healthcare Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement Programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity for Education Reimbursement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commuter Offset (Specific locations)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ping is the collective sum of all our individual experiences, backgrounds and influences and we pride ourselves in growing and learning together. We are committed to building an inclusive and diverse environment where everyone’s individuality is respected and everyone has an Identity. In recruiting for new colleagues, we welcome the unique contributions you can bring and encourage you to be your best self.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer.&amp;nbsp; All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex including sexual orientation and gender identity, national origin, disability, protected Veteran Status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a> 6300 Sales Engineering

Senior Director, Head of Quality & Responsible Person for Encaleret, International &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Mavericks Wanted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;When was the last time you achieved the impossible? If that thought feels overwhelming, you might want to pause here, but if it sparks excitement...read on&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;In 2015, we pioneered a “moneyball for biotech” approach, pooling projects and promising early-stage research from academia together under one financial umbrella to reduce risk and unleash innovation. This model allows science and small teams of experts to lead the way. We build bridges to groundbreaking advancements in rare&amp;nbsp;disease, and&amp;nbsp;develop life-changing medicines for patients with unmet needs as fast as humanly possible. &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Together we define white space, push boundaries, and empower people to solve problems. If you&#39;re someone who defies convention, join us and work alongside some of the most respected minds in the industry. Together, we&#39;ll&amp;nbsp;ask&amp;nbsp;&quot;why not?&quot; and help reengineer the future of biopharma. At BridgeBio, we value curiosity and experimentation—including the ethical &amp;amp; thoughtful use of AI to improve clarity, speed, and quality of work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Director, Head of Quality &lt;span style=&quot;font-size: inherit;&quot;&gt;&amp;amp; Responsible Person&lt;/span&gt; for Encaleret, International, leads the quality organization of BridgeBio Pharma Europe B.V. and reports to Senior Vice President Quality. As the Responsible Person, the role carries personal accountability under EU GDP for the entity&#39;s distribution activities: release for distribution, recalls, and products that are authentic, correctly stored and transported, and traceable. The role is independent of Commercial Operations, Manufacturing and Supply Chain, with an unrestricted right of escalation to the entity&#39;s full board. She/he leads and develops the entity&#39;s quality team, maintains the entity&#39;s quality management system, developed with the affiliate quality leads from existing BridgeBio frameworks, and leads WDA licensing, inspection readiness and subsequent MIA readiness, if needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the named Responsible Person on the WDA: release for distribution, recall decisions, and GDP compliance of the entity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take final disposition decision on returned, rejected, recalled or potentially falsified products (an RP decision under GDP), in consultation with BridgeBio&#39;s Global Quality Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and coordinate returns, rejections, suspected falsified products and recall operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approve return to saleable stock&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that customers are entitled to receive the products prior to shipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the WDA registration remains current with the commercial supply chain setup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the accuracy of quality records and that GDP requirements are implemented and maintained in the quality management system, as required for the WDA license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the WDA application and IGJ inspection readiness&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure data integrity and own the entity&#39;s internal audit (self-inspection) program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the GDP quality agreement matrix: contract service providers, 3PLs, distributors and intercompany interfaces&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and write standard operating procedures in BridgeBio’s document management system in accordance with the GDP requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure there is a training program for BridgeBio staff working under GDP and ensure that the relevant staff members are trained on GDP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in GDP vendor qualification program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform quality review of assigned quality events such as deviations, change controls, supplier notifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform distribution release for finished goods received from the contract manufacturing organization, which can include review of temperature, shipping and receiving documentation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be responsible for and be directly involved in product complaints from the EU and ROW markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide GDP and QA related support and intelligence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be available and reachable 24/7&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Other QA/Quality Person related responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead and develop the entity&#39;s quality team: deputy RP, QA compliance/QMS, and QA operations/GDP; and QP, if needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and maintain the entity&#39;s GDP-compliant quality management system by adopting existing BridgeBio quality frameworks, adapted to the entity&#39;s license requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the affiliate quality leads to resolve quality issues and keep the intercompany interfaces effective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare subsequent MIA readiness (QP recruitment, import, API GMP verification, and batch-certification processes), if needed&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in updating CMC sections of regulatory and quality documents as needed&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in regulatory inspections&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in internal and external project team meetings&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and review governing procedure (e.g., SOPs, WIs, etc.), where necessary&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Where You’ll Work&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a Netherlands-based role that will require 30% travel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who You Are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in pharmaceutical quality, including significant GDP / distribution quality experience; prior appointment as (or eligibility to be) a Responsible Person strongly preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading regulatory inspections with EU competent authorities (IGJ preferred)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience of managing third party vendors (CMOs, CTLs, 3PLs, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior relevant knowledge and experience related to the distribution of medical products&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of supply chain concepts, supplier management, inventory&amp;nbsp;management&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge of US/EU GMPs /GDPs and associated guidance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working in a highly regulated environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven leadership of quality teams; experience building quality functions or systems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS/MS degree preferably in operations, science, pharmacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Documented GDP training and the education and experience to be accepted as Responsible Person by the Dutch authorities (Farmatec/IGJ)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Skills&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding the EU and particularly IGJ regulations in relation to the wholesale distribution of medicines&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English language; written/spoken in Dutch language, preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong planning and time management skills with ability to prioritize workload&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills, with keen attention to detail&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of data concepts and enterprise resource planning (ERP) systems e.g., SAP&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ready to embrace company core values and diverse corporate culture&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Rewarding Those Who Make the Mission Possible&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have high expectations for our team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market leading compensationHybrid work model - we value your flexibility in how you work, but encourage time in the office to strengthen our culture, collaboration, and sense of community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We provide career development through regular feedback, continuous education and professional development programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We celebrate strong performance with financial rewards, peer-to-peer recognition, and growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a global company, our comprehensive benefits may vary based on location.&amp;nbsp; &lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We have high expectations for our team members. We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
