Senior Category Lead Modern Art &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Catawiki, every day brings the extraordinary! Whether it’s &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/en/c/583-sports-memorabilia&quot;&gt;Daniel Ricciardo’s Formula 1 Car&lt;/a&gt;, a &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/en/c/579-fossils&quot;&gt;Woolly Mammoth’s Skeleton&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/en/l/10035805&quot;&gt;Lady Gaga&#39;s Jumpsuit&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/en/c/583-sports-memorabilia&quot;&gt;Usain Bolt’s running shoe&lt;/a&gt;, we encounter exceptional objects every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a one-of-a-kind marketplace for buying and selling special objects. Each week, more than 100,000 unique items are auctioned, all carefully curated by our passionate in-house experts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Having sold over 25 million unique objects, our mission is to become the world’s most popular destination for special objects. As a growing, diverse and sustainable scale-up, we proudly live by three core values. If these values resonate with you, we’d love to explore how you can join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taking ownership and driving impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being open to change and feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being passionate about our mission and our customers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Special objects are the final frontier of e-commerce. As Senior Category Lead for Art – Primary Market, you’ll bring structure and consistency to the team’s day-to-day work. You’ll turn priorities into clear plans, strengthen how work moves across the team, and help each person take ownership of outcomes. Alongside this operational focus, you’ll support the Senior Category Manager in translating the category vision into practical initiatives that improve the experience for buyers and sellers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll create an engaged team culture built on trust, clear expectations, and accountability, helping people build on their strengths and grow in their roles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You’ll also coordinate with Sales, Marketing, and other relevant teams to deliver cross-functional improvements and keep the category’s priorities moving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create a clear operating rhythm:&lt;/strong&gt; Turn category priorities into practical plans with clear owners, milestones, and regular follow-up so work moves forward reliably.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve day-to-day operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Clarify workflows and handovers, spot bottlenecks early, and help the team resolve blockers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build team ownership and accountability:&lt;/strong&gt; Set clear goals and expectations, coach team members to take responsibility for their work, and help them use their strengths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthen engagement and development:&lt;/strong&gt; Hold regular 1:1s, give timely feedback, and support each person’s growth in partnership with the Senior Category Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use performance insights to guide action:&lt;/strong&gt; Monitor category results, identify risks and opportunities, and coordinate focused actions with relevant teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translate strategy into delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the Senior Category Manager’s vision by coordinating cross-functional initiatives from planning through execution and review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identify category growth opportunities:&lt;/strong&gt; Use market and performance insight to spot where the category can grow, then work with relevant teams to turn promising opportunities into practical initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; You have a strong track record of creating structure, setting priorities, and ensuring reliable execution in a category, sales, or commercial team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team leadership and coaching:&lt;/strong&gt; You help colleagues perform at their best through clear goals, regular feedback, coaching, and support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership and accountability:&lt;/strong&gt; You set clear expectations, follow through on commitments, and encourage others to take responsibility for outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Organised project delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; You coordinate cross-functional work, manage dependencies and timelines, and keep stakeholders aligned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical judgment:&lt;/strong&gt; You use data and customer or market insight to identify issues, set priorities, and evaluate results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear, constructive communication:&lt;/strong&gt; You build trust, share context, give direct feedback, and adapt your communication to different stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interest in contemporary art:&lt;/strong&gt; You bring a genuine interest in contemporary art and the primary art market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we work in the Art Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re a supportive, friendly Art team&lt;/strong&gt; that works together to tackle ambitious growth challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll work across Art – Primary Market&lt;/strong&gt;, supporting the Direct from the Artist and Photography categories with clear day-to-day priorities and coordinated delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll collaborate with Sales, Marketing, HR, and relevant partner teams&lt;/strong&gt;, agreeing owners and next steps so decisions turn into action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll report to the Senior Category Manager in Art – Primary Market&lt;/strong&gt; and take part in the Art cluster’s management discussions, sharing updates, aligning on priorities, and raising blockers early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you&#39;ll be&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferably this role is hybrid,&amp;nbsp; based in Amsterdam. You’ll work from our Amsterdam HQ at least two days per week.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;text text-align-left &quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You&#39;ll Love Working with Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create a visible impact &lt;/strong&gt;by working at scale in a global organisation serving millions of customers across 80+ categories. In our flat structure, every role has a broad scope and directly impacts both our customers and the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn and grow&lt;/strong&gt; through our Learning &amp;amp; Development initiatives, including clear development plans and mentorship programmes to support your career progression.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A culture of connection defines us&lt;/strong&gt;. We’re a passionate, diverse team of 800+ Catawikians representing 60+ nationalities. We foster an inclusive and queer-friendly environment where everyone is encouraged to bring their full self to work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Celebrate life’s moments with us. &lt;/strong&gt;You’ll receive a €100 Catavoucher when you join, a €50 Catavoucher on your birthday, and an extra day off each year to “Pursue Your Passion&lt;strong&gt;”&lt;/strong&gt;. We also offer additional leave for key work anniversaries and important life events. Benefits may vary by location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Offices and Way of Working&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Our vibrant offices in Amsterdam and Lisbon are designed to inspire collaboration. Most Catawikians operate in a hybrid setup, combining office-based and remote work, with a minimum of two days per week in the office, unless a role is explicitly stated as fully remote or fully office-based.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interested?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Apply with an English CV and Cover Letter. By applying, you agree to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/conditions/applicant-privacy-policy.pdf&quot;&gt;Catawiki’s Applicant Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; If you’re excited about this role but don’t meet every requirement, we still encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support the review of your application. AI may help us assess how your experience matches the requirements of the role, but hiring decisions are always made by our recruitment team&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Category Management  Amsterdam

Senior Director, HR - Field Operations (Europe) &lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role: What&#39;s in the Box&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly strategic, operational, and empathetic &lt;strong&gt;Senior Director, Human Resources – Field Operations (Europe)&lt;/strong&gt;. In this critical leadership role, you will serve as the principal HR Business Partner to the SVP of Europe Operations while providing strategic direction and mentorship to a distributed team of Site HR professionals across our European fulfillment centers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will bridge the gap between high-level operational strategy and on-the-ground employee experience. The ideal candidate thrives in a fast-paced, complex logistics or manufacturing environment, deeply understands European labor dynamics, and possesses the executive presence to challenge, coach, and partner with senior supply chain leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do: The Recipe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Business Partnering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the dedicated HR Business Partner and trusted advisor to the SVP, Europe Operations, aligning human capital strategy with broader business and operational goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive organizational design, workforce planning, and change management initiatives across the European operations network to ensure scalable, efficient, and agile structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and guide senior operational leadership on talent density, performance management, succession planning, and inclusive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Field HR Leadership &amp;amp; Team Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor, and develop a high-performing team of Site HR Managers, Directors, and HRBPs embedded within our local fulfillment centers across multiple European countries (e.g., Germany, UK, Netherlands, France, Sweden, and Norway).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a cohesive, collaborative HR community across the region, ensuring best-in-class HR service delivery, consistency in policy application, and a unified company culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear KPIs and metrics for the Field HR team, utilizing data to track retention, engagement, and operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Labor Relations, Works Council &amp;amp; Employee Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect a proactive employee relations strategy tailored to a blue-collar, high-volume operational workforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate complex European labor laws, partnering with local HR and legal teams to manage relationships with representation wherever applicable.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spearhead engagement and retention initiatives for frontline workers, ensuring a safe, inclusive, and rewarding workplace environment in our fulfillment centers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational HR Excellence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Centers of Excellence (Talent Acquisition, Total Rewards, Shared Service) to build customized programs for Field Operations, including competitive hourly wage structures, peak-season hiring strategies, and frontline leadership training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standardize and optimize core HR processes across European sites while respecting local nuances and compliance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion HelloFresh’s data-driven culture by analyzing employee feedback, turnover data, and absenteeism trends to implement targeted interventions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring: The Ingredients &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 12+ years of progressive HR leadership experience, with a minimum of 5 years leading HR functions in high-volume, multi-site Supply Chain, Fulfillment, Manufacturing, or Logistics environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Partnering:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven track record of operating as a strategic HRBP to C-suite or SVP-level operations leaders, with the ability to influence without authority and drive systemic change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pan-European Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep understanding of European labor laws, compliance standards, and significant experience negotiating and collaborating with Works Councils and trade unions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Exceptional team leadership skills with experience managing, scaling, and empowering remote/distributed HR teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical Acumen:&lt;/strong&gt; A heavily data-driven approach to HR. You rely on metrics and analytics to identify root causes, build business cases, and measure the success of people initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agility &amp;amp; Resilience:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, and dynamic environment where ambiguity is common and speed is critical.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Languages:&lt;/strong&gt; Business fluency in English is required; proficiency in an additional European language (e.g., German, Dutch, French) is highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer: The Toppings&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape the future of food:&lt;/strong&gt; Play a key role in transforming how millions of people eat as we grow into a global food solutions company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive transformational change:&lt;/strong&gt; Your decisions will have a direct and immediate impact, helping to shape strategy, scale teams, and redefine leadership in a rapidly evolving business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build a global brand:&lt;/strong&gt; Create deeper, more sustainable connections with our customers, putting them at the heart of every decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefit from long-term wealth creation:&lt;/strong&gt; Your compensation is heavily weighted toward equity, directly aligning your personal success with the company&#39;s future through our Virtual Stock Option (VSO) and Restricted Stock Unit (RSU) plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Thrive in a high-performance environment:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with ambitious, intellectually curious peers on a global scale, enjoying an environment built for empowerment and speed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a> People  Amsterdam

Business Development Director – Supply Chain Center of Excellence (CoE) &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 41, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #666e99;&quot;&gt;What Cognite is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 41, 255);&quot;&gt;Relentless&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(102, 110, 153);&quot;&gt;to Achieve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cognite operates at the forefront of industrial digitalization, building AI and data solutions that solve the world’s hardest, highest-impact problems. Our Moonshot is bold: unlock $100B in customer value by 2035, and redefine how global industry works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Field / Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; Approximately 50% (Client sites, etc)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Cognite&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cognite is a global industrial Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) company enabling the full-scale digital transformation of heavy-asset industries. Our core software product, Cognite Data Fusion (CDF), powers companies with contextualized OT/IT data to develop and scale solutions that increase safety, sustainability, and operational efficiency while driving revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Business Development Director within our Supply Chain Center of Excellence (CoE)&lt;/strong&gt;, you will drive Cognite’s growth by winning new Supply Chain business within accounts headquartered in your territory. Operating as a subject matter expert, you will leverage deep domain insights to help customers transform their supply chain value chain using Cognite Applications and the Cognite Data Fusion Platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Territory &amp;amp; CoE Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and execute a targeted territory strategy to accelerate bookings growth and secure high-impact supply chain clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pipeline Generation:&lt;/strong&gt; Actively prospect and leverage your personal network to generate pipeline, providing compelling &quot;commercial insights&quot; on optimizing the supply chain value chain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Complex Sales Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead extended territory teams (including pre-sales and technical experts) through complex enterprise sales cycles to exceed bookings targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Value-Based Selling:&lt;/strong&gt; Quantify ROI and present strong business cases to help enterprise executives justify software investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner-savvy:&lt;/strong&gt; work with partners to qualify and progress their pipeline, and drive joint engagements on qualified opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deal Negotiation:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the Account / Engagement Leader in negotiating favorable pricing and commercial terms with C-level executives by demonstrating the long-term strategic value of Cognite’s solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with internal Product Management and Marketing teams to feed real-market supply chain insights back into product strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Hygiene &amp;amp; Forecasting:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the Account Leaders and their First Line Managers in accurately forecasting monthly/quarterly bookings and maintaining up-to-date account records in &lt;a href=&quot;http://salesforce.com&quot;&gt;Salesforce.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge, Skills, Abilities (KSAs) &amp;amp; Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Competencies:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain &amp;amp; Industry Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep domain expertise in complex Supply Chain operations for Energy, Manufacturing or Power Utilities verticals. Understanding of Production operations and industry x.0 initiatives is also required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Value Selling:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to sell value and build quantified ROI frameworks for prospective buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Informal Leadership, Influence &amp;amp; Autonomy:&lt;/strong&gt; High degree of self-motivation, time management, and ability to informally lead and effectively influence cross-functional deal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Stellar presentation, written, and verbal communication skills tailored for C-suite engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge &amp;amp; Technical Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise Software/SaaS:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven mastery of selling complex analytics or data platforms (e.g., AI, Big Data, Data Warehousing, Business Intelligence, Machine Learning).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Ecosystems:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with modern data architectures and tools, such as Big Data frameworks (Hadoop, Spark, Hive, BigQuery), Data Warehouses, and Machine Learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
